WEBVTT

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.040
Hello.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:28.420
Nice to meet you. You're Kasane, right?

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:33.140
I'm Naomi. We're to be
sisters starting today.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:36.970
That makes me the big sister

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:40.230
and you the little sister, I guess.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:43.150
I hope we'll be friends, Kasane.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.080
S-Sis?

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:33.360
<i>A crime in reality</i>

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:34.660
<i>For Heaven's sake</i>

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.580
<i>Accepts any fake</i>

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:38.990
<i>And disappears</i>

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:42.080
<i>Piling the eternity in fantasy</i>

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:43.620
<i>Won't take it at all</i>

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:44.710
<i>I get sick</i>

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:46.630
<i>A girl looking back</i>

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:49.050
<i>Casts the miracle</i>

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:52.010
<i>Into the instant world </i>

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:56.890
<i>Did you lie?</i>

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:58.720
<i>Did you lie?</i>

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:01.810
<i>Spit the venom </i>

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:06.560
<i>I know why</i>

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:10.150
<i>I've found a game of ecstasy</i>

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:12.780
<i>Red Criminal gets life</i>

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:15.240
<i>I've never been in love</i>

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:21.080
<i>Don't know when I started</i>
<i>getting sick of this world</i>

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:22.660
<i>We will fly</i>

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:25.500
<i>Someday I won't be crying</i>

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:30.340
<i>I've been sacrificing myself</i>

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:32.760
<i>Not to hurt anybody</i>

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:49.020
Conspiracy

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:27.810
S-Sis?

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:33.530
Kasane!

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:59.180
Never let the Red Strings
escape your grasp.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.730
On your feet if you can fight!

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:11.440
Nagi, you okay?! Nagi!

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:30.710
Sis!

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:41.390
Kasane?!

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:44.850
Stop! If you don't...

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:56.940
Wait! Sis! Sis!

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:57.780
Enough!

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:01.740
Let me go! Naomi is...

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:06.080
Wh-What the--?
What the hell just happened?

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:08.790
Naomi turned into...

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:10.750
I don't understand.

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:16.340
Let me go!

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:17.550
Gemma!

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:22.300
I'm glad you're all safe.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.220
Major General Fubuki?!

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:26.680
Seto and Kyoka platoons are safe, too.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:28.600
The Others were eliminated.

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:30.890
Yeah, but what about...?

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:32.520
You mean Naomi?

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:38.690
Listen, everyone, I want you to keep
what you saw here today between us.

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:39.780
Huh?

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:41.450
What do you mean?

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:47.080
Exactly what I said. It's for
your own protection, as well.

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.240
Our own protection?

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:51.040
But what about Naomi?

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:52.830
Naomi...

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:56.170
She died in battle.
That's what I'll report.

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:57.670
Died in battle?

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:58.960
But...

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.630
Naomi's not dead.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:02.170
Understood.

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:03.220
Gemma!

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:05.340
Major General's orders!

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.890
Sorry about this, Gemma.

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:12.810
Wait! Kasane!

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:15.730
Going somewhere?

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:19.110
Don't go rogue in the middle of an op.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:28.910
Kasane!

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:31.910
Fubuki, I'll go on ahead.

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:33.120
Right.

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:44.050
It seems Nagi's been wounded.

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:45.720
Take him in for treatment.

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:48.350
Gemma, I'll leave the rest to you.

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:49.810
Yes, sir.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:55.560
Tsugumi, keep an eye on Kasane.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:56.770
Okay.

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:13.040
Naomi was so strong and kind.
It's not fair.

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:22.710
Such losses are to be expected in the OSF.

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:26.010
We'll just have to soldier on.

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:29.800
Damn those Others.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:34.180
How can I slack off now if she's gone?

00:07:38.230 --> 00:07:39.810
Kasane.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:54.080
Why'd it have to be an OSF platoon member?

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:56.580
And Yuito's platoon, no less?

00:07:56.580 --> 00:08:00.250
Please leave them to me.

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:04.170
I'll make sure they keep quiet.

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:09.510
Very well. I'll leave this to you,
Major General Spring.

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:11.390
Thank you.

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:28.820
Sis.

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:35.990
"Message received. Play it?"

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:50.000
Playing video

00:08:40.670 --> 00:08:44.840
I received the report
about Naomi dying in battle.

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:47.670
Why didn't you tell me?

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:50.590
Our darling Naomi is...

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:53.050
We couldn't refuse when she was scouted.

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:56.890
My only choice was to
put her in your hands.

00:08:56.890 --> 00:09:00.190
But it seems my trust was misplaced.

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:02.440
What fools we were.

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:07.440
I don't want to hear from you again.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:28.840
Going to report what happened to Naomi?

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:37.220
It was Seiran that made off with Naomi.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:43.310
They are the only ones that can
return her to human form.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:45.980
They won't kill her.

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:48.150
You have my word.

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.530
Return her to human form?

00:09:50.530 --> 00:09:55.450
You're saying I should believe you, even
though we don't know what happened?

00:09:55.450 --> 00:10:00.040
And you <i>won't </i>believe me, even though
we don't know what happened?

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:04.210
Even if we were to rescue Naomi now,
she'd be killed as an Other.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:09.960
Don't tell anyone what I just said.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.220
Otherwise, not only Naomi,

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:15.340
but you yourself will be in danger.

00:10:18.310 --> 00:10:20.850
You mean you'll kill me?

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:25.060
It's not me you need
to worry about. It's them.

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:30.860
Don't trust those New Himukans.

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:55.430
Kasane! Are you all right?

00:10:55.430 --> 00:10:58.100
You were there.

00:10:58.100 --> 00:11:01.890
So what I'm gonna say
won't break the gag order.

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:08.360
Seiran has Naomi?!

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:12.650
The OSF is hiding something.

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:20.870
Oh, yeah. I wanted to show you something,
but I don't know if it will help.

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:29.670
No, I meant what's inside of here.

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:31.630
An ampule?

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:34.260
I found them in the abandoned subway.

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:36.180
Is it some kind of medication?

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:39.640
It's got Seiran's mark on it.

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:42.350
I've seen this before.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:48.730
At your house?

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:51.520
Why would this have been there?

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:54.940
In any case, it might be a clue.

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:57.700
We should keep this between us. Agreed?

00:11:57.700 --> 00:11:59.070
Yeah.

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:03.620
I'm sorry about Naomi.

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:08.750
I knew that Other was her, but--

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:10.210
Enough!

00:12:10.210 --> 00:12:12.460
I'm going to bring her back.

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:15.510
Just see that you don't get in my way.

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:23.760
This may sound like bluster,
but I want to help if I can.

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:27.560
Bluster, huh?

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:30.440
Still, I thank you.

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:34.530
What about Nagi?

00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:38.110
I haven't heard from him
since he was hospitalized.

00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:46.790
Like me, he was in the volunteer faction,
and we started hanging out at the academy.

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:54.170
As a member of the Sumeragi Family,
no matter where I go, I'm seen as special.

00:12:56.590 --> 00:13:01.590
But with Nagi, it was totally normal,
even natural.

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:05.260
Well, maybe not normal.

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:08.100
It was like best buds from the start.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:12.190
But Nagi's the reason I made it this far.

00:13:12.190 --> 00:13:15.520
I hope we'll be friends, Kasane.

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:22.820
Kasane.

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:26.290
Commander Seto.

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:27.910
Are you okay?

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:28.950
Yes, sir.

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:31.620
You sure? Don't overdo it.

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:34.290
You needn't worry. I'm fine.

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:36.880
It's not you I'm worried about.

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:44.140
When soldiers get in over their heads,
it puts their comrades at risk.

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:48.350
It's not just you.

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:53.060
You have Kyoka and your platoon members.
Don't ever forget that.

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:54.440
Yes, sir.

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:56.900
As long as that's clear. Carry on.

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:13.120
Are you sure about this?

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:14.750
Relax.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:18.170
This is a surveillance system blind spot.

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:20.800
Our preparations are nearly complete.

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:23.130
And the destruction of the OSF?

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:25.890
It's proceeding as planned.

00:14:26.850 --> 00:14:31.350
At last, this country will fall
by our own hands.

00:14:36.400 --> 00:14:37.610
What the--?!

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:39.690
Is this even possible?

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:55.620
The MOA is forecasting an Others
event unprecedented in scale.

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:02.460
It will occur within a 10-kilometer radius
centered on Kunad Highway.

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:07.090
The entire OSF will be dispatched
to counter the threat.

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:10.470
All civilians in the area have been
ordered to evacuate.

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:13.300
"Emergency!"

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:14.010
Quickly!

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:14.690
Keep moving!

00:15:14.690 --> 00:15:17.690
--It can't be that bad.
--The Others appeared in Kunad, not here.

00:15:17.690 --> 00:15:18.980
You must evacuate!

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:20.730
All troops, move out!

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:22.400
Minakami Platoon, come forward!

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:24.240
Sakaki Platoon, come forward!

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:26.200
Kyoka, see you there.

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:28.280
Yes, be careful.

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:30.080
Where's Gemma going?

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:32.910
There's a huge number of Others this time,

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:36.250
so he's taking command of
his own special detachment.

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:38.540
Sounds like a lotta work.

00:15:42.630 --> 00:15:43.840
Kagero?

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:46.760
What? I'm just chomping at the bit.

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:49.180
Kasane. You sure you're okay?

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:54.100
Yeah, I remember what Commander Seto said.
I won't get in over my head.

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:58.020
I must stay alive, at least till
I can bring Naomi back home.

00:15:58.020 --> 00:15:59.400
Right.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:12.200
Commander Seto! You guys!

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:13.410
Nagi?!

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:16.790
They released you from the hospital?

00:16:16.790 --> 00:16:17.660
Yeah!

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:19.710
You sure... you're okay?

00:16:19.710 --> 00:16:22.670
Huh? What's the deal, Tsugumi?

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:28.970
Were you really that worried about me?
I mean, jeez, gimme a break.

00:16:28.970 --> 00:16:30.300
Commander Seto!

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:33.560
Private First Class Nagi Karman,
returning to duty!

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:36.100
It's about time. Good to have you back.

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:38.480
Out of the hospital
and onto the battlefield.

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:41.520
The OSF really works us to the bone.

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:44.860
This is the perfect way
to get back in shape!

00:16:44.860 --> 00:16:46.070
Nagi.

00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:48.740
Welcome back.

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:50.950
Now, enough chit-chat.

00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:51.780
Time to go.

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:53.080
Yes, sir!

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:57.160
Nagi, you sure you're all right?

00:16:57.160 --> 00:17:00.000
I was wounded, but I'm fine now.

00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:02.250
See?

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:06.630
That's not what I meant.
Um, what about Naomi?

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:10.260
I was shocked to hear
she was killed in action.

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:13.890
But I can't fall into a funk
about it forever.

00:17:13.890 --> 00:17:16.640
Killed in action? No, she's alive.

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:17.560
Huh?

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:22.900
Well, she's alive if you consider
being an Other a form of life.

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:25.270
Come on, what the hell
are you talking about?

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:27.900
What do you mean she's an Other?

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:32.320
If that's a joke, it's not even funny.

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:35.200
What if Kasane hears you?

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:41.120
We're about to battle the Others
to protect New Himuka.

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:44.210
I know it's hard, but we gotta
keep looking straight ahead.

00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:46.090
Come on, let's go.

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:51.800
Nagi... What in the world happened to you?

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:13.030
Commander Seto, shouldn't we
be nearing the point in the forecast?

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:16.620
We've encountered a few
Others so far, but that's it.

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:19.830
This place should be swarming with them.

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:22.410
We can call it a day if this keeps up.

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:25.580
Yes, it's far too quiet.

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:30.840
Wataru, gimme an update
on the surrounding area.

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:33.930
It doesn't look anything
like what the forecast said.

00:18:33.930 --> 00:18:35.840
Was there some sort of mistake?

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:38.890
I'll confirm with the MOA and--

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:41.180
Wataru? Come in, Wataru.

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:43.230
Haruka? Haruka!

00:18:43.230 --> 00:18:46.770
Commander Seto, come in! Commander?!

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:50.610
Wataru! I lost contact with Kyoka Platoon!

00:18:50.610 --> 00:18:52.990
Wait, could this be...?!

00:18:52.990 --> 00:18:55.740
Are we being jammed?!

00:18:55.740 --> 00:18:57.280
Tsugumi?

00:18:57.280 --> 00:19:00.040
Commander, we're surrounded!

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:09.710
Aren't they OSF?

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:14.050
Were there other platoons
dispatched to this point?

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:20.680
Gemma?

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:28.900
Gemma? What the hell is this?

00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:31.360
We were just about to call it a day.

00:19:31.360 --> 00:19:33.570
So don't start piling on the work.

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:35.900
Care to explain, Gemma?

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:38.620
Forgive me, Kyoka.

00:19:38.620 --> 00:19:43.660
Seto, I can't believe you're involved
in such horrific research.

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:45.410
What are you talking about?

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:47.120
So you're gonna play dumb?

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:49.290
Like I said, what are you talking about?

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:51.210
What the hell is this?

00:19:52.630 --> 00:19:54.800
What is going on?

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:03.930
I'd beat a hasty retreat if I were you.

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:04.850
Luka!

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:08.310
Luka Travers!

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:13.150
Or are you so cocky that you think
you can defeat two Septentrions?

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:15.650
Care to explain, Luka?

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:17.110
I'll explain later.

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:20.620
I'll draw the attention of those
OSF units while you escape.

00:20:20.620 --> 00:20:24.370
If I were your foe,
the same could be said of me.

00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:32.000
Commander Karen!

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:33.250
Karen!

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:35.880
Luka, I'm not surprised you're here.

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:38.840
Go! Leave my brother to me!

00:20:39.930 --> 00:20:41.220
Weak!

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:49.310
Brain field?!

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:01.780
Sclerokinesis, electrokinesis,
<i>and </i>aerokinesis?!

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:03.490
Remember?

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:08.540
Commander Travers can copy
and use other psionics' powers.

00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:11.880
Brain... Eater!

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:17.970
Commander Travers,
are you behind all this?

00:21:17.970 --> 00:21:22.140
This nation...
New Himuka is deceiving us all!

00:21:34.900 --> 00:21:36.570
Gemma,

00:21:36.570 --> 00:21:42.530
is there anything you can tell me
about my sister, Naomi?

00:21:42.530 --> 00:21:43.450
Naomi?

00:21:43.450 --> 00:21:44.830
What's this about?

00:21:48.040 --> 00:21:52.170
I knew it. New Himuka's government
has something to do with--

00:21:52.170 --> 00:21:53.920
Kasane?!

00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:56.550
What is she talking about?

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:04.800
Answer me. Answer me, Gemma!

00:24:09.210 --> 00:24:11.970
Red Strings
